Subject: [PATCH 4/9] test(roles): the request renames roles, the one
 definition still compiles them
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Red: a-team-not-a-person (culprit 0e2ff096)
  the roles are COMPILED from one definition, not retyped
    pinned `export const ROLES = ${JSON.stringify(ROLES.map` and the old
    two-name import
  and the build message tells the owner the roles exist at all
    pinned `${describeRoles(false)}`

Decision: P for both. 0e2ff096 added rolesForRequest(): «admin and
receptionist roles» renames owner/staff (en, noteEn) over ROLES; the
permission lattice is ROLES' own. ApiProjectTool compiles
fileAuthJs(roleSpecs) from `const roleSpecs = rolesForRequest(...)`, and
the build message describes the same roleSpecs in both languages. Nothing
is retyped; the one definition still feeds server and message.

The COMPILED test now follows that chain (fileAuthJs(roles = ROLES),
rolesForRequest -> roleSpecs -> 'auth.js': fileAuthJs(roleSpecs)) and
asserts the behaviour: a renaming request changes the names (proof the
comparison is not empty) and leaves [key, write, ownRowsOnly, manageUsers]
identical to ROLES. The message test reads describeRoles(..., roleSpecs)
UNDER each message heading — a bare match was being satisfied by the
README's own describeRoles(true) call.

Non-vacuity:
  roles-repermission (roles.ts): renaming staff also sets ownRowsOnly:false
    ✕ the roles are COMPILED from one definition, not retyped
    "staff", true, -  true, +  false,   RESTORED: sha256 identical
  roles-retyped (ApiProjectTool.ts): server table typed by hand
    ✕ the roles are COMPILED from one definition, not retyped
    Expected pattern: /export const ROLES = \$\{JSON\.stringify\(roles\.map/
    RESTORED: sha256 identical
  roles-message-defaults (ApiProjectTool.ts): EN message describes
  describeRoles(false) instead of the compiled list
    ✕ and the build message tells the owner the roles exist at all
    Expected pattern: /Team — three roles, accounts made from inside the system:\n\$\{describeRoles\(false, roleSpecs\)\}/
    RESTORED: sha256 identical

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CSeapUrWatvdumdAwyPuqV
